    {
        "title": "Context Engineering: The Hidden Skill Behind Production-Ready AI",
        "venue": "NextGen Data 2026 | Barcelona, Spain",
        "date": "March 2026",
        "sortDate": "2026-03",
        "category": "conferences",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/nextgen-data-2026.png",
        "description": "<p>Presented at NextGen Data 2026 in Barcelona (virtually), this talk made the case that most production AI failures aren’t model failures — they’re context failures. Drawing an analogy to exam preparation (reading too much, going blank mid-question, or writing great answers to the wrong question), the session introduced context engineering as the critical discipline for anyone shipping AI to production.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>The demo-to-production gap: why perfect demos become unreliable deployments (hallucinations, latency, spiralling costs)</li><li>The context window as your application’s RAM — instructions, knowledge, and tool outputs</li><li>Common context failure patterns and how to diagnose them</li><li>Practical context strategies for production systems</li><li>Cutting-edge patterns emerging from the field</li><li>Open source tools and arsenal for context engineering</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "Slides",
                "icon": "fas fa-file-pdf",
                "url": "./assets/data/resources/202603_NextGenData2026_ContextEngineeringTheHiddenSkillForProductionReadyAI.pdf"
