                "label": "LinkedIn Post",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
                "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/tezan-sahu_nextgendata2026-contextengineering-ai-activity-7441347937152000000-STwW"
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "title": "Context Engineering: The Make-or-Break Skill for Production AI",
        "venue": "PyConf Hyderabad 2026",
        "date": "March 2026",
        "sortDate": "2026-03",
        "category": "conferences",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/context-engineering-pyconf26.jpg",
        "description": "<p>Delivered at PyConf Hyderabad 2026, this talk brought context engineering to the Python community — showing why the gap between a working demo and a reliable production AI system almost always comes down to how you fill the context window. The session used the memorable analogy of exam preparation gone wrong to drive home why ‘the model isn’t broken, the context is.’</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Production reality check: perfect retrieval vs. hallucinations, snappy responses vs. unbearable latency</li><li>Defining the discipline: the context window as your application’s RAM (instructions, knowledge, tool outputs)</li><li>Common context failures and diagnostic approaches</li><li>Practical context strategies for Python-based AI applications</li><li>Cutting-edge patterns and the open source arsenal</li></ul>",
