    {
        "title": "Stop Hoping, Start Evaluating",
        "venue": "Future World Conversations | Future World Alliance",
        "date": "March 2026",
        "sortDate": "2026-03",
        "category": "community",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/stop-hoping-start-evaluating-future-world-conversations.png",
        "description": "<p>Delivered at Future World Conversations, this talk challenged the AI community to move beyond ‘looks good enough’ and embrace systematic evaluation for AI agents. The session walked through the anatomy of an AI agent, a structured building process, and then deep-dived into why evaluations are the missing piece in most agent development workflows.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Anatomical elements of AI agents: LLMs, system prompts, tools &amp; functions, memory &amp; context, guardrails, and the orchestrator</li><li>A practical 5-step agent building process</li><li>Introduction to evals — what they are, why they matter, and how to design them effectively</li><li>Evaluation-Driven Development (EDD) as a methodology for building reliable agents</li><li>Tools and resources to get started with agent evaluation</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "Recording",
                "icon": "fas fa-video",
