    {
        "title": "The Authenticity Paradox: Engineering Soul into the Intelligent Age",
        "venue": "Manifest 2026 | Framer, Creative Community & Microsoft",
        "date": "February 2026",
        "sortDate": "2026-02",
        "category": "community",
        "type": "🎤 Panel Discussion",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/manifest-2026.png",
        "description": "<p>Participated in a cross-disciplinary panel debate at Manifest 2026 (organized by Framer, Creative Community &amp; Microsoft), exploring the tension between AI-driven scale and human authenticity. The discussion challenged conventional thinking about what happens when AI products optimize for the wrong metrics, and argued for taste-driven development as a counterbalance to velocity-obsessed engineering.</p><p><strong>Key Themes Discussed:</strong></p><ul><li>Authenticity breaks when AI scales — not because the tech fails, but because we optimize for the wrong things</li><li>Goodhart's Law is eating AI products: when trustworthiness becomes a score, systems test well but feel hollow</li><li>The trade-off future generations will regret: trading architectural integrity for velocity (10x faster builds, 10x technical debt, 1/10th the thinking)</li><li>The case for taste-driven development: spec-driven contracts and conscious overrides that bake judgment into systems from day one</li><li>The gap between vibe-coded prototypes and production — where authenticity dies</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "LinkedIn Post 1",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
