    },
    {
        "title": "From Prompting to Proving: Eval-Driven AI Agent",
        "venue": "Hello Intelligence 2026 | Microsoft AI Innovators Hub, Hyderabad",
        "date": "January 2026",
        "sortDate": "2026-01",
        "category": "community",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/hello-intelligence.png",
        "description": "<p>Delivered at Hello Intelligence 2026 (Microsoft AI Innovators Hub, Hyderabad), this talk made the case that the best AI teams don't move fast because they guess better — they move fast because they measure better. The session covered the anatomy of AI agents, a systematic building process, and deep-dived into why evaluations are the missing piece in most agent development workflows.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Anatomy of AI agents and their core building blocks</li><li>A 5-step process to build agents systematically</li><li>Why evals are not optional — turning intuition into data, and data into compounding progress</li><li>Evaluation-Driven Development (EDD) as a methodology</li><li>Tools and frameworks to get started with agent evaluation today</li><li>Practical advice: start small, test against reality (not happy paths), and let measurement guide you</li></ul>",
