    {
        "title": "Eval-Driven Agent Development",
        "venue": "AgentJam | Global AI Community, Hyderabad",
        "date": "November 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-11",
        "category": "community",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/agentjam_global_ai_hyd.png",
        "description": "<p>Delivered at AgentJam (Global AI Community, Hyderabad), this talk shared a practitioner's perspective on Evaluation-Driven Development for AI agents. Drawing from hands-on experience building and shipping agents, the session presented a framework for making agent quality systematic rather than aspirational.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Evals velocity = product velocity: the fastest AI teams measure daily, not just build daily</li><li>Start small, scale systematically: begin with 10–20 representative cases, then grow the eval suite in response to real failure modes</li><li>Mix your methods: rule-based checks for precision &amp; reproducibility + LLM-as-judge for nuance and ambiguity</li><li>Design for the real world: inject noise, embrace ambiguity, test edge cases — not just textbook inputs</li><li>Measurement over hope: turning \"I think it works\" into \"here's the data — it works 87% of the time, and here's where it breaks\"</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "LinkedIn Post",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
                "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/tezan-sahu_globalaihyderabad-aiagents-evaluation-activity-7398251300787904513-qQra"
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "title": "Do Agents Do What Developers Say?",
        "venue": "MLADS+ Agents Conference | Microsoft (Virtual)",
        "date": "November 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-11",
        "category": "conferences",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/do-agents-do-what-developers-say.jpeg",
        "description": "<p>Presented at the MLADS+ Agents Conference (Microsoft), this talk introduced Instruction-Following Accuracy (IF-Accuracy) — a developer-centric evaluation framework for measuring how faithfully AI agents follow the business logic encoded in their instructions. The work addressed a critical gap: existing eval rubrics judge user experience, but agentic systems need developer instruction fidelity.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>The motivation: developers encode custom business logic via instructions and expect it to be followed — but only ~70% of instructions were being followed vs. 95% in benchmarks</li><li>Root causes of the gap: ambiguous instructions, conflicts with system prompts, tool failures, and attention bottlenecks</li><li>The IF-Accuracy computation pipeline: atomic instruction breakdown, turn-wise applicability assignment, conversational instruction-following analysis, and hierarchical aggregation</li><li>Analytics &amp; visualization: turning raw scores into actionable insights via dashboards</li><li>Real customer impact: improving IF-Accuracy to 90+%, unblocking large-scale agent deployments</li><li>How to leverage the framework: standalone tool, internal evaluation platform integration, and extensibility to other agent platforms</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "LinkedIn Post",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
                "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/tezan-sahu_aiagents-evaluation-instructionfollowing-activity-7397991272969347072-JKoK"
            }
        ]
    },
    {
