        "category": "universities",
        "type": "🔬 Workshop",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/ieee-leadership-summit.jpeg",
        "description": "<p>A full-day hands-on workshop at the IEEE Leadership Summit, taking students on a structured journey from AI essentials to building and evaluating production-grade AI agents. The morning covered foundational concepts and agent building with Microsoft Agent Framework, while the afternoon focused on creating comprehensive evaluation suites using the Azure AI Evaluation SDK.</p><p><strong>Learning Objectives &amp; Topics:</strong></p><ul><li>Understanding what AI agents are, when to use them, and how they differ from chatbots</li><li>Core elements of agentic systems: fundamentals, architectural patterns, and design tradeoffs</li><li><strong>Lab 1:</strong> Building functional AI agents with Microsoft Agent Framework</li><li><strong>Lab 2:</strong> Creating comprehensive evaluation suites with Azure AI Evaluation SDK</li><li>Evaluation-driven development: using evals to iteratively improve agent behavior</li><li>Production deployment considerations and best practices</li></ul>",
