    {
        "title": "Intro to Evals: The Why, What & How of Making Agent Quality a Habit",
        "venue": "AI4All | CAPE, Microsoft (India)",
        "date": "October 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-10",
        "category": "microsoft",
        "type": "🔬 Workshop",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/intro-to-evals.png",
        "description": "<p>Co-presented with Akhil at Microsoft's AI4All initiative (CAPE team), this workshop demystified evaluation-driven development for AI agents. Drawing from months of building, breaking, and refining agents, the session reframed evals not as unit tests but as human judgment, scaled — and walked attendees through a practical approach to making agent quality systematic.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Evals ≠ traditional QA: unit tests check \"does it work?\" — evals ask \"does it work well, in the messy, ambiguous, human way we expect it to?\"</li><li>Start manual: define what \"good\" looks like before automating with LLM-as-a-judge</li><li>Evals encode expertise: turning PM and domain expert intuition into repeatable signals that scale</li><li>Not all evals are worth automating: focus effort on high-impact, high-frequency user journeys</li><li>Tools amplify but don't replace thinking: using platforms to automate evals at scale, but only after defining clear scenarios, assertions, and success criteria by hand</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "LinkedIn Post",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
                "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/tezan-sahu_ai-aiagents-evaluation-activity-7388435536564142080-_9vn"
            }
        ]
    },
