        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/gen-ai-aaruush25.jpg",
        "description": "<p>A comprehensive Gen AI workshop at Aaruush ’25 (SRMIST, Chennai), delivered across two tracks. The first track covered AI agent fundamentals, agentic design patterns, and the rise of agentic protocols, with live demos building single-agent and multi-agent systems using Microsoft’s AutoGen framework. The second track focused on AI model customization and fine-tuning.</p><p><strong>Track 1 — AI Agents Unleashed:</strong></p><ul><li>AI agent fundamentals: what makes agents smart (autonomy, goal-orientation, context-awareness)</li><li>Agent architecture and agentic design patterns</li><li>Rise of agentic protocols (MCP, A2A)</li><li>Live demos: building single-agent and multi-agent systems with AutoGen</li><li>Taking AI agents to production</li></ul><p><strong>Track 2 — AI Model Finetuning:</strong></p><ul><li>Why customize AI models: domain specificity, reduced prompt engineering, edge deployment, privacy</li><li>Demystifying technical jargon: SLMs, Chain of Thought, reasoning models, LoRA, QLoRA</li><li>Live demo: fine-tuning a Phi-4 model for medical reasoning tasks</li></ul>",
