        "description": "<p>A 6-hour, two-day hands-on workshop for Product Space, designed specifically for 40+ Product Managers — most of whom hadn't coded in 5+ years. The session took participants from zero to building multi-agent systems with Microsoft's AutoGen framework, proving that PMs don't need to be full-stack developers to prototype and orchestrate AI agents.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Why PMs need to understand agentic frameworks beyond prompting</li><li>The AI Agent Stack: tools that matter today</li><li>Design patterns for AI agents</li><li>AutoGen fundamentals and hands-on setup</li><li>Single-agent evolution: instructions → tools → memory → RAG</li><li>Multi-agent orchestration: getting agents to collaborate</li><li>Production-ready systems: UI, observability, and edge cases</li></ul><p>The highlight was watching seasoned PMs rediscover their coding spark — bridging product vision with technical possibility in real-time.</p>",
