    {
        "title": "Model Context Protocol (MCP): From Buzzword to Build-Ready",
        "venue": "SkillUp AI | The Garage, Microsoft (India)",
        "date": "August 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-08",
        "category": "microsoft",
        "type": "🔬 Workshop",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/mcp-from-buzzword-to-build-ready.png",
        "description": "<p>Co-presented with Pankaj Aher (Principal Software Engineer, Microsoft IDC) at SkillUp AI for 200+ attendees, this workshop cut through the hype around MCP (Model Context Protocol) and showed attendees how to actually build with it. The session combined architectural deep-dives with multiple live demos, covering everything from MCP primitives to creating production-ready agents that use MCP servers.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>AI agents and tool use — why tools are essential for useful agents</li><li>Introduction to MCP: what it is, its architecture, and core primitives (with demos)</li><li>Ecosystem overview of available MCP servers</li><li><strong>Demo:</strong> Creating an M365 Copilot Agent with MCP Tools using Agent Toolkit (ATK)</li><li><strong>Demo:</strong> Creating an M365 Copilot Agent with Remote MCP Servers using Copilot Studio</li><li><strong>Demo:</strong> Using MCP Servers with GitHub Copilot in VS Code</li><li>Security in MCP — threat models and mitigation strategies</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "Slides",
                "icon": "fas fa-file-pdf",
                "url": "./assets/data/resources/202508_SkillUpAI_MCPFromBuzzworkToBuildReady.pdf"
            },
            {
                "label": "LinkedIn Post",
                "icon": "fab fa-linkedin",
                "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/tezan-sahu_ai-microsoftgarage-mcp-activity-7366680957396910080-ZExq"
