        "description": "<p>A hands-on workshop for 100+ students during SIT Hyderabad's industrial visit to Microsoft, bridging theory to practice with live AI agent building and model fine-tuning. The session showed how to build declarative agents in M365 Copilot using Agents Toolkit (ATK) with access to MCP tools, followed by a walkthrough of AI model customization and fine-tuning techniques.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Building declarative agents in M365 Copilot using Agents Toolkit (ATK)</li><li>Integrating MCP tools into Copilot agents for extended capabilities</li><li>Why customize AI models: domain specificity, reduced prompt engineering, edge deployment, privacy</li><li>Demystifying technical jargon: SLMs, Chain of Thought, reasoning models, LoRA, QLoRA</li><li>Live demo: fine-tuning a Phi-4 model for medical reasoning tasks</li></ul>",
