    {
        "title": "Vibe Mode On! Flip the Switch to AI-First Programming",
        "venue": "Microsoft M365 Core",
        "date": "July 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-07",
        "category": "microsoft",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/vibe-mode-on.jpg",
        "description": "<p>Delivered to Microsoft M365 Core, this talk explored the vibe coding revolution — the shift from AI-assisted to AI-first programming. The session covered industry trends, the evolving AI coding toolkit, practical challenges like hallucinations and the context conundrum, and shared battle-tested best practices and error handling strategies for getting the most out of AI-powered development tools.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>What vibe coding actually is: an AI-first, conversational style of programming that goes beyond AI-assisted coding</li><li>Industry trends and the growing AI coding toolkit: IDE integrations, browser-based generators, CLI tools, and Microsoft's internal tools (GitHub Copilot, Bandish, SWE Agent, Rubber Ducky)</li><li>Navigating major challenges: the hallucination monster and the context conundrum</li><li>The \"AI is Dumb\" fallacy — why treating your AI co-pilot like a day-one intern produces better results</li><li>8 universal best practices: start with a plan, work incrementally, use Git religiously, debug with error messages, add codebase instructions, reference API docs explicitly, use annotated screenshots, and keep experimenting with models</li><li>Error handling strategies: Revert &amp; Re-Prompt, Call Out Patterns, Debugging User Flows, and Visual Debugging with UI Screenshots</li><li>Tool-specific tips for GitHub Copilot and SWE Agent</li><li>What's next: agent clusters, agent fleets, and our evolving roles in an AI-first era</li></ul>",
        "links": []
    },
    {
        "title": "Intern Global Hackathon Kickoff",
        "venue": "The Garage (India) & The University Recruiting Team, Microsoft",
        "date": "July 2025",
        "sortDate": "2025-07",
        "category": "microsoft",
        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/intern-global-hackathon-kickoff.jpg",
        "description": "<p>Mentored 500+ Microsoft interns at IDC Hyderabad during the Intern Global Hackathon kickoff, in collaboration with The Garage and The University Recruiting Team. Alongside fellow mentors, the session tackled questions on tech stacks, time management, and how to build a hackathon prototype while juggling an internship.</p><p><strong>Core Advice Shared:</strong></p><ul><li>Time-box your creativity: 2–3 hour focus blocks beat scattered all-nighters</li><li>MVP over perfection: solve the problem first, polish comes later</li><li>Team with opposites: the best ideas are born at intersections</li><li>Solve the problem, not the stack: impact matters more than the number of frameworks used</li><li>Reuse what exists: APIs and open-source are your friends</li><li>Fail fast, pivot faster: if it's not working by Day 2, switch it up</li><li>Build with an AI-first mindset: use GenAI to mock UIs, generate code, and brainstorm features</li></ul>",
        "links": [
