        "type": "🗣️ Talk",
        "image": "./assets/images/speaking-engagements/agents-assemble.jpg",
        "description": "<p>Presented at the 24xAI Conference, this talk demonstrated how to build powerful AI workforces by orchestrating multiple specialized agents using Microsoft’s AutoGen framework. The session moved from foundational concepts to live coding demos, showing how agents can collaborate, decompose complex tasks, and leverage tools to achieve goals beyond the reach of any single agent.</p><p><strong>Key Topics Covered:</strong></p><ul><li>Why multi-agent systems: the limitations of single-agent architectures</li><li>AutoGen framework: architecture, agent types, and conversation patterns</li><li>Building single-agent systems with tool use</li><li>Orchestrating multi-agent teams: task decomposition, delegation, and collaboration</li><li>Live coding demos with the companion GitHub repository</li></ul>",
        "links": [
            {
                "label": "GitHub Repo",
                "icon": "fab fa-github",
