        "description": "<p>A candid video interview with Sundar Srinivasan (VP, Microsoft Search &amp; AI), where Tezan shared his journey as an Applied Scientist on the Bing Autosuggest team, his diverse passions beyond work, and his learnings at Microsoft. The conversation touched on work culture, mentoring, work-life balance, and advice for early-career professionals.</p><p><strong>Topics Discussed:</strong></p><ul><li>Role at Microsoft: working on Bing Autosuggest — making search suggestions more relevant and personalized for millions of users</li><li>Passions beyond code: painting (three solo exhibitions), singing (YouTube covers), technical writing, and authoring the bestselling book \"Beyond Code\"</li><li>Microsoft's learning culture: sessions, workshops, conferences, and the non-technical growth in communication, personal branding, and adaptive leadership</li><li>Mentoring culture at Microsoft: being on both sides of the table — how mentoring helps articulate complex ideas simply</li><li>Advice for early-career professionals: channelize your energy by finding the right platform, environment, and people to maximize impact</li></ul>",
